# Centrifugo & data refresh

## Rule

**Do not add automatic refetches after mutations or on org switch.** After the initial bootstrap, list/detail refresh must come from Centrifugo events via `UserCentrifugeListener`.

## Bootstrap (allowed once)

- `UserProvider` / `OrganizationProvider`: fetch on mount only.
- `WorkflowProvider` / `EndpointProvider`: fetch **once** when an active org first appears. On org switch, clear stale lists and wait for Centrifugo — do **not** call `fetchWorkflows` / `fetchEndpoints` in a `useEffect` tied to `activeOrganization`.

## After mutations

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — refetch after mutate
await createWorkflowStep(...)
await loadSteps()

// ✅ GOOD — mutate only; Centrifugo refills (optimistic UI OK for delete/move)
await createWorkflowStep(...)
```

Optimistic UI (remove from state immediately, rollback on API error) is allowed for deletes/moves.

## Event → fetch map

Handle new events in `lib/centrifugo/types.ts` + `user-centrifuge-listener.tsx`. Debounce list refreshes (~500ms).

| Event | Action |
|---|---|
| `user.*` | `GET /api/users/me` |
| `user.active_organization_changed` | orgs + workflows + endpoints (+ me via user.*) |
| `organization.created` | orgs + workflows + endpoints |
| `workflow.created/updated/deleted` | `GET /api/workflows` |
| `endpoint.created/deleted` | `GET /api/endpoints` |
| `endpoint.updated` | single `GET /api/endpoints/:id` if editing that id, else list |
| `step.created/updated/deleted` | `GET .../workflows/:id/steps` (page subscribers) |
| `connection.created/deleted` | `GET .../workflows/:id/connections` (page subscribers) |

Steps/connections: use `subscribeWorkflowStepsRefetch` / `subscribeWorkflowConnectionsRefetch` on the workflow page — scoped by `workflowId` from the event.

## Do not

- Refetch workflows/endpoints in providers when `activeOrganization` changes (duplicates Centrifugo).
- Poll or `setInterval` for lists.
- Invent event types not emitted by the backend.
